# netsurf: grid repeat(auto-fill|auto-fit) sized by the container; numeric grid-area/-row/-column with spaces (patch 206, with 206-libcss)
# Generated 2026-10-07
# Base: seleron/vitabrowser f352150 (patch stack through 205)
#
# Two grid bugs found by a geometry probe against Chromium:
#
# 1. grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fill, minmax(100px, 1fr)) -- the
#    card-grid idiom -- got its column count at CSS-rewrite time from a
#    900px viewport guess (fixes362), capped at 8, so a 350px grid had 8
#    columns of 35px. The rewrite now emits one marker ("afN", "atN",
#    "apN"; 206-libcss packs them) for repeat(auto-fill|auto-fit,
#    minmax(Npx, ...)) and repeat(auto-*, Npx) in column lists, and
#    layout_grid expands it against the grid's own width:
#    n = floor((W + gap) / (N + gap)), at least 1, at most 16; auto-fit
#    collapses the empty tracks (never more tracks than in-flow items);
#    minmax tracks become fixes1214's px-floor + 1fr tracks, plain
#    lengths px tracks. emit_one_track lets the markers through (it folds
#    unknown tokens to 1fr). Row lists keep the old expansion (the rows
#    parser knows no markers). Other auto-repeat forms (several tracks,
#    non-px minimums) keep the old estimate.
#
# 2. macsurf__grid_parse_int_or_minus1 stopped right after the digits, and
#    every caller then tests for '/', so `grid-area: 2 / 1 / 3 / 3` -- the
#    form the grid-template-areas pass emits and most authors write --
#    lost everything after its first number: named areas never spanned
#    ("c c" was one column) and numeric placements with spaces fell back
#    to auto-placement. It now skips the whitespace after the number.
#
# Test: testpages/pages/CSS-grid-autofill.html (GRIDFILL206, 8 checks,
# Chromium 8/8; 1/8 without 206-208): 3 columns of 110px in 350px and the
# 4th item wrapping, 6 columns in 700px, auto-fit stretching 2 items,
# auto-fill keeping empty tracks, fixed 150px tracks, a "c c" area
# spanning, grid-area: 1 / 2 / 2 / 4, grid-column: 1 / 3. Full gate: see
# docs/build-loop-state.md.
